{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>All the gold.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said: why did he mention what they did with the silver, but not mention what they did with the gold of the wave-offering? And he answered: behold, he mentioned that the menorah was a talent of gold, and likewise the cover and the gold of the ark and the incense altar. But this is not correct, for the menorah was entirely gold, but not so the ark — only overlaid with gold, inside and out — and likewise the incense altar, and the table, and the poles, and the boards, and the bars — all overlaid with gold. And the cover was entirely gold, and according to what we received from our fathers, it was one talent, for its length was great and its width was great. And in my opinion, he mentioned what they did with the silver because it is the silver of the atonement-money, and behold, he mentioned that upon the silver of the levy stood the tabernacle, which encompasses all the vessels — and this is a remembrance for the children of Israel. And who can reckon how much gold overlaid all the vessels of the tabernacle:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:51.739047327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}